AnyMakerCatalogMod

Inspired by Electron's posts, and their .dll implementation method.
The name trainer is kind of null now. Now exe's or anything to run.

Setup
1. Unzip the folder.
2. Copy dinput8.dll next to game.exe in your AnyMaker installation folder.
3. Start the game, load a world, and open your inventory. The catalog appears beside it.

Use
Browse Items or Components, or search directly. Click an image to add the item. Hover for its description. Settings includes a toggle for separate color and skin variants.
To remove it, close the game and delete this dinput8.dll from the game folder.

How It Works
The catalog runs inside the game as a DirectInput proxy DLL. It forwards DirectInput calls to the Windows DLL and uses the game's item routines. 
No game files are edited. Adding items can change your world.

Unofficial mod; not endorsed by the game developer.

Change Log

- Added each Keycard as an item (S01, S02, S03) 
- Fixed some icon issues
